<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Albert II, Duke of Mecklenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1590">1590</a>–<a href="/years/1636">1636</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as John Albert II of Mecklenburg-Güstrow</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-ii-duke-of-mecklenburg">Albert II, Duke of Mecklenburg</a>, shared rule of Mecklenburg with his brother Adolf Frederick I, and their partition of 1621 created the Duchy of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustrow">Güstrow</a>. Both brothers were deposed in 1628 when the emperor gave Mecklenburg to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albrecht-von-wallenstein">Albrecht von Wallenstein</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years War</a>. Swedish intervention restored them in 1631.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-albert-ii-duke-of-mecklenburg.jpg" alt="John Albert II, Duke of Mecklenburg" width="320" height="597" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Blok · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JohannAlbrechtII.Mecklenburg.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
